{"type":"text","timestamp":1790255755487,"sessionID":"ses_f2c769b84ffes8LS5rfITv9aQQ","part":{"id":"prt_0d38ef0d1001wfgOOIJTMp3zw6","messageID":"msg_0d38eac3d001JJmPuJVWipJim5","sessionID":"ses_f2c769b84ffes8LS5rfITv9aQQ","type":"text","text":"Implemented the layered muzzle flash prefab in [muzzle_flash_effect.tscn](/workspace/scenes/effects/muzzle_flash_effect.tscn).\n\n- Root uses `generic_effect_handler.gd`, targets the `MuzzleFlash` OmniLight3D, and sets the fade duration to **0.2 seconds**.\n- `SmokeParticles` uses zero gravity, a radial `GradientTexture2D`, and a `StandardMaterial3D` with particle billboard mode.\n- `MuzzleFireLeft` and `MuzzleFireRight` emit opposing one-shot bursts using the supplied shader and double-sided QuadMesh draw passes.\n- [Main](/workspace/scenes/main.tscn) instantiates the effect with clearer camera framing and a dark preview background.\n\nAlso corrected the [shader’s transparency mask](/workspace/assets/shaders/muzzle_flash.gdshader) to remove visible rectangle edges and overlapping depth artifacts.\n\nVerified in **Godot 4.4.1** using front and reverse captures: both fire bursts render, smoke expands and fades, and the effect cleans itself up. Final runs completed without scene or script errors.","time":{"start":1790255755473,"end":1790255755474},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0f1b6bec8046b93f016ab5227e64348197a61a6929e1e69511","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
